\newlabel{fig:enriched-heatmap}{{1}{3}{Core and peripheral argument complexes emerge from enriched distributional hom-values. Relation graph visualizing \(\mathcal {C}(A,B) \in [0,1]\) among all eight case roles. Strong relations (solid edges) cluster into two groups: the \textbf {core argument complex} (NOM--ACC--DAT, linked by transitive and transfer morphisms) and the \textbf {peripheral complex} (LOC--INS--ABL, linked by spatial and instrumental relations). GEN bridges both via possessive modification. Weak relations (dashed edges) connect VOC---its peripheral isolation reflects the pragmatic rather than syntactic function of direct address. These hom-values yield the similarity matrix \(Z\) (\autoref {eq:eq-5-4}) and categorical magnitude of \autoref {sec:enriched-categories}. Generated programmatically from the \protect \texttt {EnrichedCategory} class}{fig:enriched-heatmap}{}}
\@writefile{snm}{\beamer@slide {fig:enriched-heatmap}{3}}
